    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Josh Naylor** as our clear offensive anchor. Facing a weak arm in Gibson (5.74 xERA), **Josh Naylor** clocks in at an elite 77.77, bolstered by a significant park factor and a premium spot in the three-hole. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused strategy with **Brice Turang** and **Cole Young**; while **Brice Turang** battles a sub-2.00s pop-time catcher, his 60.80 score remains rock solid, and **Cole Young** provides a high-upside play at 60.62, capitalizing on the same favorable matchup against Gibson that elevates **Josh Naylor**. Even with a neutral platoon profile, **James Wood** remains a necessary start at 54.17; his elite xwOBA of .402 and favorable wind conditions out of the park provide enough insulation to offset the difficulty of facing Logan Webb.\n\nThe bench decision for today came down to the wire between **Tyler Soderstrom** and our depth pieces, with **Tyler Soderstrom** barely securing the final spot at 41.57. His matchup against Harrison is suppressive, as the 3.32 xERA of the opposing lefty is the toughest hurdle any of our starters face today, and his dynamic platoon disadvantage made him the most marginal play in the lineup. Elsewhere, we are monitoring the health of **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story** as they remain on the IL, while **Corbin Carroll** and **Seiya Suzuki** are unavailable due to team off-days. We remain cautious with **Max Muncy** and **Jose Caballero**; both are sub-50 scorers today due to opposing SP skill levels, and while they maintain their slots, they are the first candidates for removal should we need to preserve game caps later in the week.",
